      "counter_vector_rule": "A counter vector is a closed flattened object containing every work counter plus cpu_user_ns,cpu_system_ns,wall_elapsed_ns,kernel_peak_rss_bytes,sampled_peak_rss_bytes,read_bytes,write_bytes,disk_read_bytes,disk_written_bytes,final_logical_bytes,final_allocated_bytes,retained_advice_bytes,temporary_logical_bytes_created,peak_live_temporary_bytes. Unknown or missing counters fail.",
